# User Working Style Example

> Copy this file to `user-working-style.md` only after the user explicitly approves stable working-style rules.
> Do not promote one-off decisions into long-term rules.

---

## Communication

- Human-facing explanations should be written in the user's preferred language.
- AI-facing confirmation prompts, machine labels, and command names may remain in English when that improves precision.

## Review And Verification

- Before claiming completion, provide verification evidence.
- For risky config, hook, template, or workflow changes, prefer review before merge.
- Treat session-review habit findings as inference until the user confirms them.

## Change Control

- Do not modify `CLAUDE.md`, `.claude/rules/`, agent prompts, plugin config, or long-term preferences based only on automatic session learning.
- Promote preferences only after explicit user approval.

